libwebrtc
---------

The Windows build (district-call's `livekit` feature, in District AI core for
Rust, which district-ffi turns on for Windows) statically links libwebrtc, as
this project builds it for the LiveKit Rust SDK: LiveKit's own Windows recipe
and pinned sources for release webrtc-a545de4 of github.com/livekit/rust-sdks,
with every patch that recipe applies, built by scripts/build-libwebrtc.ps1
without the H.264 and H.265 codecs or FFmpeg. The archive is
webrtc-win-x64-release.zip in release libwebrtc-a545de4-audio-win-1 of this
repository, SHA-256
a9b991e7baff30c32423507d82a8d80bee6b85ec0812b45a4e83a5af2d78ec02, which is the
pin in scripts/fetch-libwebrtc.ps1. The archive's LICENSE.md holds the full
licence text of every component it contains (WebRTC, BSD-3-Clause, and its
third-party code), and a distribution of the app must ship it with the binary.
